6|0@socialism^1439998246#cu8by6x:inthemouthsofmaggots$:I edited my block quote to exclude the section on Clinton's attempt to establish trade liberalization. Clearly I'm not for free market trade of any sort. I meant the act of isolating China from internationalist relations, in this case the international market place, is a nationalistic, imperialistic, and capitalist act. Protectionism fosters the idea of nationalism by reinforcing the notion of borders, I do not think protectionism is imperialist (clearly), I just think its nationalistic. 
